 to the to the Z piece like that  because they line up so when you flip it  just make sure that that line is  horizontal and then you could lay the  piece on top of the Z piece so again the  S piece is flipped over and made sure  that this line is horizontal and placed  on top of the Z piece and you should see  the two pieces form what looks like an X  in the middle so we need to interlock  the bottom piece flaps into the top  piece as you'll see if you lay the flaps  down you'll see where they need to go  this flap needs to be put underneath  here so what you do is you just lift  this up and you place that flap  underneath there this piece needs to go  underneath here so just lift it up and  we could tuck this one underneath there  so you should have a piece that looks  just like that and just make really good  creases and make sure everything is nice  and flat then we could flip the model  over and as you'll see we have two  pockets here we have one pocket here and  we have another pocket here this piece  is going to fit into this pocket and  this piece on the left is going to fit  into the pocket on the right so all we  need to do is just tuck the tip of the  flap into the opposite pocket tuck the  left flap into the right pocket you  might need to open this up a little with  a pen cap or something tuck it in there  and then you could tuck the right flap  into the left pocket so just open this  up a little bit and you should be able  to tuck that right in just like that  make sure everything is flat and you  have finished your origami ninja star to  throw this shuriken just fling it like a  frisbee at this angle
 

